ome with the regular m1  ship  at the base 1800 price and then have an  upgrade option  for the m1x but i feel like paying 1800  for the same m1 chip as you get in a  macbook air is a bit of a rip  off but then again if you really think  about it the current  1800 intel based macbook pro already  comes with  16 gigs of ram and 512 gigs of storage  at the base price so if apple matches  those specs  for the new 14 inch base model you're  really only paying a hundred dollars  more  for the new redesign and the new display  compared to a similarly configured  current m1 macbook pro which isn't that  bad at all  so the m1 chip and the base 14 inch is  still a possibility  and then of course the 16 inch macbook  pro will get the m1x  at the base 2400 price but either way  i'm expecting new redesigned macbook  pros at wwdc  and if you totally disagree with my  speculation and reasoning  let me know down in the comment section  below but if you agree with me  click that circle above to subscribe for  more videos like this one  check one of those two out right there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video  you
 

